---
title: "migrate_v1_to_v2 (Sui Framework: deny_list)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_bag: bag_entry = deny_list.lists[per_type_index]
    q_get_bag --> q_check_exists: check denied_addresses.contains(per_type_key)
    q_check_exists --> q_empty: does not exist
    q_empty --> q_get_config: elements = empty vector
    q_check_exists --> q_remove_v1: exists
    q_remove_v1 --> q_get_elements: elements = denied_addresses.remove(key).into_keys()
    q_get_elements --> q_cleanup_loop: for each addr in elements
    q_cleanup_loop --> q_dec_count: denied_count[addr] -= 1
    q_dec_count --> q_remove_zero: if count == 0, remove from table
    q_remove_zero --> q_cleanup_loop: next addr
    q_cleanup_loop --> q_get_config: cleanup done
    q_get_config --> q_migrate_loop: get per_type_config
    q_migrate_loop --> q_set_v2: for each addr in elements
    q_set_v2 --> q_migrate_loop: set AddressKey(addr) = true in config
    q_migrate_loop --> [*]: migration complete

    note right of q_remove_v1
        INV-001: V1 entries removed and re-created in V2 format
        INV-002: denied_count correctly decremented during migration
        INV-003: V2 entries take effect at next epoch
        INV-004: migration is one-way (V1 data deleted)
    end note
